# HiVi documentation maintenance

Before implementing backend features, read `docs/Backend_Flow.md`.

## After every meaningful backend change, update docs in the same task

| If you changed… | Update |
|-----------------|--------|
| API routes, request/response | `docs/Backend_Flow.md` § API reference |
| Auth, OAuth, JWT, CORS, security rules | `docs/Backend_Flow.md` § Security |
| New/changed entities or tables | `docs/Backend_Flow.md` § Database schema |
| Backend packages, services, schedulers | `docs/Backend_Flow.md` § Backend layout |
| Community, opportunities, Reddit behavior | `docs/Backend_Flow.md` § relevant feature section |
| Render/env vars, prod profile | `docs/Backend_Flow.md` § Configuration / Deployment |

## Do not skip

- New endpoints → add to `Backend_Flow.md` before finishing
- Security rule changes → update public/protected route lists in `Backend_Flow.md`

## Entry point

- `docs/Backend_Flow.md`
- Cursor summary: `AGENTS.md`

Do not create additional docs in `docs/`; extend `Backend_Flow.md` only.
